From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Open HTTP and RTSP media asynchronously by URL.

The MPEG-TS log in #748 stops at scheme_handler_BeginCreateObject before
any demuxer is created. Non-MP4 HTTP sources still use
URLOpenBlockingStreamW there, which waits for the download to finish.
An endless transport stream cannot finish, and even finite downloads
block the caller before the asynchronous resolver work is queued.

Use the existing IO work item to open all HTTP(S) media through FFmpeg,
including TS, MKV and extensionless URLs. Preserve the existing HLS and
progressive MP4 options. Bound non-HLS network IO waits, identify live
nonseekable inputs without discarding known finite durations, and share
the existing common timestamp offset across their audio/video streams.
Only interpret AVIO opaque data as a Wine stream_context when using
Wine's own read callback; direct network inputs have FFmpeg-owned IO.

The RTSPT trace reaches the demuxer but reads the empty placeholder
bytestream. Open RTSP URLs directly as well, translating rtspt:// and
rtspu:// to rtsp:// with explicit TCP and UDP transports respectively.
Normalize only the scheme's case, leaving paths and query data intact.
Register both explicit-transport aliases with Media Foundation.

The alias registrations follow Torge Matthies
<openglfreak@googlemail.com>'s winegstreamer change, commit
67bfe239bba3755fced37ed0f1283f32713e8a75 (CW-Bug-Id: #21644), carried
by SpookySkeletons/proton-rtsp. The FFmpeg implementation here is new;
it does not import the GStreamer backend or claim its other aliases.

Add loopback resolver tests for HTTP, extensionless and common media
paths, RTSP, RTSPT, RTSPU, and mixed-case schemes. Hold the server reply
until BeginCreateObjectFromURL returns to detect synchronous network IO.
These cover routing and asynchronous failure completion, not successful
media playback or RTSP SETUP transport negotiation.

Reference: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/748
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/medfound/supported-protocols
Reference: https://ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg-protocols.html#rtsp
Reference: https://github.com/SpookySkeletons/proton-rtsp/blob/rtsp/10-33-24/patches/wine-gst/0005-winegstreamer-Add-more-RTSP-based-URI-schemes-to-GSt.patch
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@
 
 #include "mfapi.h"
 #include "mferror.h"
-#include "urlmon.h"
 
 #include "wine/list.h"
 
@@ -2801,22 +2800,9 @@
     if (cancel_cookie)
         *cancel_cookie = NULL;
 
-    if ((!wcsnicmp(url, L"http://", 7) || !wcsnicmp(url, L"https://", 8))
-            && (wcsstr(url, L".googlevideo.com/videoplayback") || wcsstr(url, L".mp4")))
-    {
-        /* The demuxer opens progressive HTTP media directly through FFmpeg. */
-        if (FAILED(hr = CreateStreamOnHGlobal(0, TRUE, &stream)))
-            return hr;
-    }
-    else if (!wcsnicmp(url, L"http://", 7) || !wcsnicmp(url, L"https://", 8))
-    {
-        if (FAILED(hr = URLOpenBlockingStreamW(NULL, url, &stream, 0, NULL)))
-        {
-            WARN("Failed to open url %s, hr %#lx\n", debugstr_w(url), hr);
-            return hr;
-        }
-    }
-    else if (FAILED(hr = CreateStreamOnHGlobal(0, TRUE, &stream)))
+    /* The IO work item opens the URL through FFmpeg. Downloading here would
+     * block BeginCreateObject indefinitely for an unbounded HTTP stream. */
+    if (FAILED(hr = CreateStreamOnHGlobal(0, TRUE, &stream)))
         return hr;
 
     hr = MFCreateMFByteStreamOnStream(stream, &bytestream);
@@ -2825,8 +2811,13 @@
         return hr;
 
     if (FAILED(hr = MFCreateAsyncResult(NULL, callback, state, &result)))
+    {
+        IMFByteStream_Release(bytestream);
         return hr;
-    if (FAILED(hr = object_context_create(flags, bytestream, url, -1, 0, result, &context)))
+    }
+    hr = object_context_create(flags, bytestream, url, -1, 0, result, &context);
+    IMFByteStream_Release(bytestream);
+    if (FAILED(hr))
     {
         IMFAsyncResult_Release(result);
         return hr;
